|~ `::binding`, the kind of the record a declaration writes into its
   scope, and the laws declared under it. ~|

:binding
  |~~ A binding is the record a declaration writes: a name with its
      page, its value and where it came from, so what is named can be
      listed and asked like data. `env` answers the bindings a reader
      declared, and `binding` the record of a name,
      `::vec/count | binding | /origin` answering `:qlang/vec`.

      It prints as a map under its tag; in the command line the record
      of `:x 5` is
      `::binding{:name :x :docs [] :value 5 :source ~(:x 5) :origin :cell-1}`.
      `:name` is the keyword it binds, `:docs` one doc for each doc of
      its slot, `:value` what the name holds, `:source` the quote of the
      step that declared it, and `:origin` the source or the cell it was
      read from. A value a host binds is a binding without a page or a
      source.
      ::link~(::bind | doc) ::link~(::any/binding | doc)
      ::link~(::qlang/names | doc)
  ~~|

:binding/holdsTheValue
  |~~ The record of a name holds its value. ~~|
  ::law~(:x |~~ One. ~~| 1 | env | /x | /value | eq 1)

:binding/holdsThePage
  |~~ The record of a name holds its page. ~~|
  ::law~(:x |~~ One. ~~| 1 | env | /x | doc | content | eq " One. ")

:binding/holdsTheName
  |~~ The record of a name holds the name. ~~|
  ::law~(:x 1 | env | /x | /name | eq :x)
